     If you're capable of achieving a wishless ascension then you
shouldn't need to ask about such things. :-)  And you didn't
specify your role or race.  For a vampire, a ring of slow digestion
was crucial for me; I couldn't count on finding or making potions
of blood and draining life from monsters wasn't reliable enough;
that left prayer, and sooner or later I'd pray too soon and end up
in serious trouble.  For roles other than archeologist, I might go
for a blessed touchstone so that I could identify and sell gems in
order to pay for shopkeeper services.  In the early game, that can
be extremely valuable.

     A few other likely choices:  amulet of flying to guard
against having a trap door drop you into the midst of trouble,
or a silver weapon to take care of the inevitable werecritters on
the mall level.  Magic candle is another possibility.  Spellbook
of magic missile is great too; that spell is very potent and in
slash'em you can trivially prevent it from ever timing out.  Or
blessed potions of gain ability; high constitution means extra
hit points whenever you gain a level so getting it early means
you'll have the bonus more times overall.

     They're all things you'll find eventually, but having one or
more of them from the very start will increase your character's
chances for survival.  I wouldn't go for an amulet of life saving;
I find that wearing one of those tends to encourage recklessness.
I'd pass on figurines to acquire angelic pets for the same reason.


